<?xml version="1.0"?>
<model>
  <name>fpv_target</name>
  <version>1.0</version>
  <sdf version="1.9">model.sdf</sdf>
  <author>
    <name>Interceptor Simulation (demo)</name>
    <email>emersonium2@gmail.com</email>
  </author>
  <description>
    DEMO-ONLY visual dress-up of the M2 AprilTag target board: the same tag
    (same pose, same 0.625 m plane / 0.5 m tag_size, same emissive_map
    material as models/apriltag_target -- see model.sdf header) wrapped in a
    primitive-built "enemy FPV quadcopter" body (dark carbon + red accents)
    so the portfolio demo video reads as an interceptor catching a drone,
    not a printed board. Detection is unaffected: the tag geometry/material
    is byte-identical to models/apriltag_target, and every added body part
    is either behind the tag plane (occluded from the approach view) or
    entirely outside the tag's footprint (see model.sdf comments for the
    per-visual occlusion proof). Used only by worlds/apriltag_demo.sdf; the
    gated worlds keep using models/apriltag_target unchanged.
  </description>
</model>
